{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jonah [D]walked through Nineveh, three days [G]wide and tall
[D]He [G]shouted forty days and then your c[D]ity's going to fall
The [A]king came [G]down from his throne and sat down in [D]the dust
And the whole [Bm]great city [D]turned around, they put [G]away their lust
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]When God saw what [D]they did, how they turned from their evil way
He [G]relented concerning [D]the disas[Bm]ter and he spared them on that [G]day
But Jonah sat [D]outside the town [A]and sulked [G]beneath a vine
He said I knew [D]you'd be [Dmaj7/C#]like this, you're [Bm]merci[D]ful and kind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Should [G]I not then care [A]about Nine[D]veh, that great c[G]ity
More than a hundred and [D]twenty thousand [Bm]people
Who do not know [A]their right hand from their left
[G]And also many ani[D]mals
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dmaj7/C#]The [Bm]little [G]plant that gave him shade, it with[D]ered [D]in a night
And Jonah cried a[G]bout the plant and said [D]it [Bm]isn't right
You [G]cared about this [D]plant, which you did not [A]la[G]bor for
I care for every soul, [D]said God, [Dmaj7/C#]and so [Bm]much more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Should I not then [G]care a[A]bout Nineveh, [D]that great city
[G]More than a hundred and twen[D]ty thousand peo[Bm]ple
Who do not know their [A]right hand from their left
[G]And also many [D]an[Dmaj7/C#]i[Bm]mals
{end_of_chorus}

